# Local commits

The user asked for local commits on a steady cadence so progress survives a Cursor window restart. This overrides the default of committing only when a message says "commit", for this project only.

- Commit locally after a finished slice: a request is done, the files are saved, and the change is whole enough to keep. Do not commit mid-edit, a broken halfway state, or an empty tree.
- Several small edits that belong to one request can share one commit at the end of that request. A long request gets a commit at each coherent checkpoint.
- Local only. Do not push unless the user asks in that message.
- Use `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git`. Do not update git config, skip hooks, force-push, or amend.
- Message style: `Cursor: …`, one or two sentences on why.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
- If the window dies before the next checkpoint, only what is already committed is safe. Uncommitted edits in the working tree can still be lost.
